## Implemented output

Four small modules in `v2/experiments/action_executor/r27/pre_contract`, reusing
unchanged runtime_closure/real_path/broker and original R21 producer bodies.

- E1: Exact pinned original rows/write_packet/marker algorithms and mutation expressions
  quantify raw bytes and known lifecycles. Pure bounded memory preview is analysis,
  not a qualifying storage substitute or execution of all six original tests.
- E2: The exact packet callsite executes through genuine OwnedBroker/HostPort and
  a closed logical temporary path. Full/four-row natural diagnostic mappings reject
  the whole JSONL before that artifact I/O; ephemeral diagnostic mapping rejects
  the whole full JSON. Both mappings are proposals only, not adopted scratch routing.
  Prefix artifacts/bytes, unchanged rejected charge, original traceback/first fault
  and absent seal are checked. Rejected bytes are test memory, not captured evidence.
  One-row uses the existing producer parameter for nine-write fidelity and delete/
  recreate/no-refund controls; it does not replace original1600-row qualification.
- E3: Source-bound entry always denies full PRE before root/child/marker dispatch.
  Booleans, mappings, count claims and candidate objects cannot grant permission.
  Genuine tempfile/pytest/native/shell routes remain named uncovered paths.
- E4: Combined regression, static/source/raw-byte preservation and independent
  verification/review. Frozen existing sources/product/dependencies are unchanged.

Previously verified genuine pytest XML, original fileConfig/logging, whole native
host-df EOF, signed fixture/parser and shared recovery flow remain covered by the
unchanged23 regression groups. The reused packet seal witnesses its old real_path
source set; new external binding separately verifies additions before/after.
Neither is full-runtime certification or a universal hostile-native-FD sandbox.

