## Root obstruction now quantified

| Source-generated payload/control | Observed size/lifecycle |
|---|---|
| Full1600 synthetic rows, samples.json | 235,440B |
| Same whole samples.jsonl write | 233,840B, not1600 source write calls |
| Four-row JSON / JSONL | 582B /578B (whole journal still exceeds512) |
| Corruption method | 35 writes /733,169B lifetime payload; final live4050B |
| Six-method known successful scratch writes | 43 explicit calls;14 lifetime files;6TemporaryDirectory roots |
| Launcher +known scratch files | At least125+14=139, before native/plugin/probe/failure additions |

Eight mutation/restore pairs, one journal truncation and summary deletion are counted.
The original cap sums surviving file sizes under the epoch; intended TMPDIR and
basetemp are inside while live. Poll/postcheck may miss deleted/overwritten bytes.
The new broker precharges lifetime attempts and packet+physical copies without refund.
These are different semantics; final live4050B is not733,169B retained history.

Genuine first-use tempfile probe/unlink/fallback/rmtree, pytest given-basetemp
mkdir/rm_rf/numbered tmp_path/current symlink, fake-shell printf and unknown plugin/
native failure writers remain unqualified. Given --basetemp does not take the
ordinary session cleanup-lock branch. synthetic_settings is a constructor, not
itself a filesystem/seed producer. Known lower bounds are not universal upper bounds.

Current32 entries/PRE32, twenty families,10MiB aggregate and16KiB metadata remain.
Earlier96/PRE64 is insufficient and NOT_ADOPTED. Existing conditional launcher
metadata forecasts exclude scratch/interleaved/error history; they are not seals
or complete fit proofs. Synthetic input copies are not genuine measurement journal/
final_samples observations; diagnostics must not silently adopt that classification.

## One next material decision, not another count-only round

Recommend a **stage-specific PRE synthetic-input variant within the SAME shared
10MiB/no-refund boundary**, with complete source-derived whole-write, lifetime-file,
metadata and native/deleted-scratch ownership domains. Preserve original whole
serialization and fail before I/O; no uncapped second plane, omission or splitting.
This is a proposed contract change requiring explicit Homeowner adoption, not
permission supplied by passing tests. Exact domain/bounds and all native writer
routes still need closure before full PRE or any campaign request.

Missing dependency/Linux/physical SQL/effect prerequisites stay separate. No install,
SQL/Docker/HTTP/load/provider/network/Git write/rebuild/executor activation occurred.
No future marker consumed; no live absence check claimed. Existing unrelated dirty
work/cache preserved; no project copy, new distDir/venv/Docker resource created.
Keep the same R27 package; preserve baseline thresholds, workload and old failed
evidence. No measured latency repair or full candidate certification has occurred.

